{"id": "EUVD-2026-108832", "enisaUuid": "7de78fea-5256-3f98-842d-595f7e0ba98b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-crypt: reject the lmk IV mode with AEAD ciphers\n\nA \"capi:\" table line that pairs an AEAD cipher with the lmk IV mode,\nfor example \"capi:gcm(aes)-lmk\" with the integrity:28:aead option,\ncauses an oops when it is loaded. lmk sets tfms_count to 64, but\ncrypt_alloc_tfms_aead only allocates one transform, so crypt_setkey\nreads past the end of the tfms_aead array and calls crypto_aead_setkey\non the values it finds there.\n\nlmk exists for compatibility with Loop-AES, which uses CBC, so refuse\nit with an AEAD cipher rather than allocate 64 AEAD transforms. The\ncheck cannot go in crypt_iv_lmk_ctr with the other lmk checks, because\nthe IV constructor runs after crypt_set_key.\n\nNote that this is not a security bug because the memory corruption can\nonly be triggered by root.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:21:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:21:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a0dab8a9d9975dec14a118b55cae2517aea5ca9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/962ce265fbf5d87afeb78cf19c12e083ab0ffeb8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a1a875614dae43b43d311bb9e7a7a70eed78efe6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40ea7dfa8cd5f9aed72a55c9ca3008aee5880e6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3195e0daf590683992edb4eed32269e569e04924"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99037"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06b777cf-eea7-36dd-ae27-6c1b39688b6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "33d2f09fcb357fd1861c4959d1d3505492bf91f8 <9a0dab8a9d9975dec14a118b55cae2517aea5ca9"}, {"id": "14a78155-a058-307e-8659-66607d1e2d4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "3b775c20-9fa5-3a98-8cd3-1dc906a52097", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "33d2f09fcb357fd1861c4959d1d3505492bf91f8 <40ea7dfa8cd5f9aed72a55c9ca3008aee5880e6f"}, {"id": "3cac32cb-945f-3b16-a19d-d35027ac85b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "4a11ab96-c3b5-3698-822c-088df757af3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "33d2f09fcb357fd1861c4959d1d3505492bf91f8 <3195e0daf590683992edb4eed32269e569e04924"}, {"id": "6c92ac6a-0544-3082-89ed-a6194a720cfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "33d2f09fcb357fd1861c4959d1d3505492bf91f8 <a1a875614dae43b43d311bb9e7a7a70eed78efe6"}, {"id": "84f2414f-e0eb-3b40-b060-0bbdc361cd6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "a311f43a-4c02-3848-bf7c-8360f023d5ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.12"}, {"id": "a3b86f57-1c45-304d-a5e8-33e80b2f7b5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b11196cb-a67b-31e3-84ae-0a118cc3dd2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "c4b80732-3e38-376b-ba13-b75877a16d24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "33d2f09fcb357fd1861c4959d1d3505492bf91f8 <962ce265fbf5d87afeb78cf19c12e083ab0ffeb8"}, {"id": "e47ffd5c-1880-361b-8cdc-15ed23314c3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3a57962d-bc41-38b9-a6c8-893f02dbe772", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}